WEBVTT

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:38.310
It's the fairyland at the bottom of the universe.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.150
Dreams in a wasteland. A town overrun with violence.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.770
The idiot's utopia.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.490
The planet people call "Endless Illusion."

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.360
Van and Wendy allowed...

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.490
the Claw to escape from the port town of Harbor Parade.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.540
The two chase after him...

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.040
even as they are tossed about by the storms of fate.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.670
But after the storm there is a calm.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.670
A most dreadful calm.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:11.010
The Vengeance Within

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.220
What? It's broken?

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.140
We went too fast and the engine died.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.640
There's no way we can catch up with a boat...

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.100
that left over 12 hours ago in such a short amount of time.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.810
You should have told me that sooner!

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.690
I know the port where they're going to.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.530
There's nothing to get worked up about.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.070
We'll have it fixed in 4 or 5 hours.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.650
You can go hang out and relax over on that island until then.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.450
We can't sleep on the boat?

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.320
You'd have to lie on the edge of the deck.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.790
And there's not much space so you'd get in the way of our work.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.790
We'll lend you a boat, so think of it as a vacation, OK?

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.330
Damnit! 4 or 5 hours?

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.420
Yeah.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:50.460
You can read a book at a time like this?

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.220
There's nothing we can do.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.390
I thought they said they were going on a long trip.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.980
They don't have shit.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.310
Hey... that's my?!

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.940
They only gave us enough gas for one way!

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:16.410
Oh no... they're thieves?!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.330
Damnit! And of all places!

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.290
What seems to be the matter?

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.500
I see. What a terrible thing to have happened to you.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.800
Every so often there are those people...

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.880
who become captives of their own greed.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.680
It is a true shame.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.100
Mister Joe Lutz...

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.850
Just call me Joe.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.350
Joe, aren't there any ports on the island?

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.190
Well, you see...

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.520
this place is my own personal property.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.610
It is?

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.820
The island had an official name...

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:54.490
but I now call it by the one I gave to it myself.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.080
Welcome to La vie en Rose.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.250
It's my villa which I built for entertaining guests.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.830
Right now only the staff and myself are here...

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.420
so please make yourselves at home while you wait for the next boat.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.880
But...

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.970
Of course there aren't any expenses for staying.

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.090
My intentions are entirely well meaning.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.800
I don't like it.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:21.810
Van!

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:23.930
Van?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.440
You must be the Van "The Devil's Poison in the Poisoned Tuxedo."

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.520
I went by that name a long time ago.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.860
I've been called Van, "the Good Person" as well.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.110
Then I must apologize.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.070
Well then, Van, is there something which you're unhappy about?

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.030
Not really.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.240
I just don't like it when people tell me that they're "well meaning."

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.450
Van! You're being rude!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:47.290
I am truly sorry if I've hurt your feelings.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:52.590
My wish is for the peace and happiness of all those who I encounter.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.210
What do you get out of it?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:59.930
I'm not concerned with gains or losses anymore.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.720
I've already made my fortune.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.430
In that case, hurry up and lend us a boat.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:07.480
There's nothing more I'd rather do than provide you with that which you desire...

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.270
but there are no boats at La vie en Rose right now.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.440
A mail carrier will be coming here in 10 days.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.690
I ask that you please...

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.900
10 days?!

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.490
Yes. Please stay here until then.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.200
I look forward to doing everything I can to entertain you as my guests.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.680
So soft!

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.990
10 days in this place.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.630
Please, relax.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.420
Yes.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.590
Excuse me...

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.180
Give me a milk instead of this.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.260
And bring me all the condiments you've got.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.690
The two people you're looking for...

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:38.570
the Claw and Miss Wendy's older brother...

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.740
I passed on the information about them to my staff in the Scenic Islands.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.410
I'm having all boats entering all harbors checked.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.490
So please set your minds at ease and make yourself at home.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:51.160
Why are you doing all this?

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.000
No matter in what form, all human encounters are fate.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.250
Given that, I devote myself entirely to whomever I am with.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:02.010
Even if it amounts to nothing more than a mere fraction of my life.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.800
Thank you.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.800
Think nothing of it.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:11.770
I'm only trying to be faithful to my own philosophy.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.150
I'm sorry about earlier today.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:20.110
That's all right. I am often misunderstood.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.440
By the way...

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.280
I'd like to ask you about something if it's all right.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.910
What is your relationship with that man...

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.700
Of course, you don't have to answer if you don't want to.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.170
No, it's OK. He's...

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.800
It's beautiful!

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.450
I see.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.200
Your bride...

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.530
I know very well how you must feel.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.040
I've lost many friends.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:16.040
You see, at one time I was involved in a conflict.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:19.290
There were those who were killed by the enemy.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.420
Those who were betrayed by their friends.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.630
Those who I buried myself.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.470
But...

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:31.010
Van, do you know what awaits you at the end of vengeance?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.970
Nothing.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:39.060
My restless body and soul arrived at that final station and...

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.440
there was nothing.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:26.110
You're an excellent tennis player, Miss Wendy.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.150
I feel refreshed!

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.660
I wish Van could have joined us.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.790
Van is back in his room resting.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.910
He's still sleeping?

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.000
Yes.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.830
But in any case, that was some great tennis you played.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.000
My brother taught me. Although he didn't teach me much.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.590
You said his name was Michael, right?

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:50.300
I wish I could meet him.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.810
We've been here 3 days already. I hope my brother's OK.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.100
Of course he is.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:00.140
He has to be with all the concern you've shown.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.560
This is just a guess but that man wouldn't have gone through...

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.440
the trouble of taking Michael away with him unless he had a reason.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.150
Which would mean he has no intention of killing him, right?

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.360
That's right!

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:13.070
Yes.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.330
The chances of him returning home safely are extremely high.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:18.830
Which would mean...

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:22.120
wouldn't you stand an even better chance of seeing him again...

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.630
if you waited in your hometown?

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:28.300
That's the only place for him to go back to and...

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:31.340
if he returned while you're out, you could end up missing each other.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.770
Nothing comes from anger and bitterness.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.900
But through friendship all things are possible.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.030
Amongst these people, there are some who were my enemies.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.860
There are some who were my friend's enemies as well.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.200
Why did you become friends with them?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.780
Because I forgave them.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.040
I saw that was the starting point for everything.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.790
I've been informed that the man is in the town of Tours.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.040
Shall I put a tail on him?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.050
Please!

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.880
How about a game?

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.590
Did you tell her?

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:17.550
Miss Wendy was tired from playing tennis earlier today...

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.100
and has already gone to bed.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.350
I'll tell her first thing tomorrow.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.720
I see.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:23.940
This calls for a drink in celebration.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:24.890
Sure.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.230
Thanks. You've been a big help.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.820
You're too open about things.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.900
So much so that you scare me.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.530
You seem to have gotten on the boat of desire.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:46.290
And that boat is heading for the depths of despair.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.050
Do you stand to gain anything by killing the Claw?

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:56.840
That's not what this is about.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:01.100
He killed Elena! I'm going to get my revenge.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.350
Is that what she would have wanted?

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.520
Or is it merely something you want to do?

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:10.610
But!

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:16.900
The person who contacted me was once my enemy.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.290
Hatred calls for more hatred.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:29.170
Out of which comes only a chain of vengeance.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.710
Which satisfies no one.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.710
You are undoubtedly pure.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:38.380
Because of this pureness, you let your hatred lead you where it may.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.810
But the woman who you loved...

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.350
wouldn't she have wanted you to forget about everything...

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.140
and live happily in peace instead?

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.100
Shut up! I don't care what you say!

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:56.320
There's one left.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.280
What are you going to do?

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:03.080
Will you put an end to it today or will you continue?

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:04.450
It's your decision.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.930
Lucky! Lucky!

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:28.810
You stay in here, Wendy.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:29.480
But...

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.560
Hurry!

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.770
Kameo, take good care of her.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.980
What about you, big brother?!

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:39.490
Don't worry about me. You just hold tight.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.740
Don't go outside.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:41.610
But you'll!

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.200
I'll be fine. I've got this with me.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.410
I'll come back no matter what.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:49.250
So don't go outside. Promise me.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:02.090
This is what I think.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:06.310
Those who entrust themselves to their own desires only lose their pride...

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.270
and make enemies.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:12.400
They don't accept anyone, thank anyone or take joy in anything.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:15.940
Ahead of them lies their own destruction.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:19.440
Something for you to think about, Van.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.040
So maybe it's better if I went home?

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.910
Yes, you probably should.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:31.540
You're more likely to find him that way.

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:36.790
We'll protect Michael and bring him to Evergreen.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.760
Van said the same thing.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.050
He also thinks it's safer that way.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:46.760
Right now he's back in his room recovering from a hangover.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.970
I see.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:58.110
Go home? She said that?

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:02.530
Yes. I'll see to it that she makes it back.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.280
Don't be ridiculous.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.870
What about her brother? What's she going to do about him?

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:11.500
He has his life, and she has hers, right?

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.880
It's something for you to consider as well, Van.

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:27.180
Yes. This is another thing I believe.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:29.810
Life is victory.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.520
Death is defeat.

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:34.190
The quiet peacefulness that keeps desire at bay...

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.690
is the key to true happiness.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:41.650
Shouldn't you be thinking about your own happiness?

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:46.160
I suppose... even if I...

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.820
Even if I didn't do it...

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.330
he would still...

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.040
because I know...

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.040
he would...

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:20.730
Elena...

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:24.860
Elena, I'm tired.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.360
Every day that you're not here.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.410
Maybe it's time for me to let you live on as a memory.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:37.540
No. You shouldn't do that, Elena.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.380
Come on, stop it.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.590
Stop it, Elena.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.060
That's right.

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:58.770
There can be no happiness for me in this world...

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.940
because Elena is gone.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.730
That was some joke!

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.110
Huh, Joe!

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.610
That's too bad.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.820
I was really hoping we could become good friends.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:14.990
You're a friend of the Claw!

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:20.500
The plan was to have you slowly rot away here, but...

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.630
you leave me no choice.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:27.670
You really do disturb the peace.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:30.130
You are our enemy!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.970
"Our?"

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.430
It's a pity, Van.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.640
I now challenge you to fight...

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:39.980
"Golden Cradle," the Armor my comrade left here for me.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:43.860
There are lots of things I need to ask you.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.690
So I'm sorry, but...

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.240
I'll have to bite the hand that feeds me!

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.500
Let's see what you've got.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.120
Wake up, Dann!

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:07.800
Launch, Golden Cradle!

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:11.680
Van!

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.260
Excuse me while I take the liberty of striking first.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.760
Sure. Go ahead.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.270
Very well then...

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.060
I'm finally sober!

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.780
You'd be happier if you'd stayed drunk.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.070
Not bad!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:37.660
Van!

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:41.830
I'm sorry but I have to laugh at you for even thinking...

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.790
you could find and kill my comrade with your level of ability.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:45.840
Joe...

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.830
You stay in here, Wendy.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.870
Just hold tight. Don't go outside.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:27.670
That man has a great cause.

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.300
You are, so to speak, the ghost of an abandoned past!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:36.090
Which means you cannot go back! You cannot look back!

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:39.350
Please don't express your desires any more!

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.640
I get your point!

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:46.650
Now hear mine.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:51.690
I'm going to beat the crap out of you and find out where the Claw is.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.530
I'll follow him all the way to the lowest pit of hell.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:57.280
I don't give a damn what you all think!

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:01.240
If I did, I'd never be content!

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.490
Yes. That's right.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:04.460
That's my desire!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:05.960
My future!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:10.500
What's wrong with me doing things my way!

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.680
Van!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.140
It's about time for me to get ready for dinner...

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:25.430
so I ask that you kindly prepare yourself.

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:28.270
You're the one who needs to be prepared!

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:30.060
You must be joking!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:43.290
Van!

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.790
Chesuto!

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.920
Well done... You sank the last ball...

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:59.260
I should have expected nothing less from the Original Seven.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:02.680
But even so, I was able to buy time for my comrade.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:07.140
Are you going to tell me where he is?!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.350
And now...

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:15.320
for my final act of friendship...

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:17.530
Excuse me.

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:18.450
What?!

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:29.960
Damnit!

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.380
- Did our master win?

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.460
- Who cares?
- Did our master win?

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.470
If we don't get out of here quick...

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:42.390
Stop the boat!

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:51.810
It looks like the Claw has other friends as well.

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:57.030
And he knows I'm coming.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.740
It's going to become even harder to track him down.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.070
Hey, Van...

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.790
We're not making a mistake, are we?

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:09.870
I don't know.

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:13.080
But even so, I'm not stopping any more.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.040
What about you?

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:25.850
I'm sorry, big brother.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:30.520
Allow me to break just one of our promises.

00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:59.270
That's when we met Joshua.

00:24:00.230 --> 00:24:03.780
He helped me out after I ran into some Armor in the mountains.

00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:08.740
He knew a lot about Armor and had a good heart.

00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:12.790
Van hated him, but we got along from the start.

00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:17.830
Yes, we did seem to have some things in common.
